			<div class="content" id="post-content-4364090">
									

<blockquote>
<p>Are the Priorihominus also intended to be the creators of SCP-1795?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>It wasn't my intention, but I <em>was</em> aware of SCP-1795 when putting together some of the ideas here. I will say that the two have undeniable thematic similarities and both involve an advanced early human presence.</p>
<p>To add to this, even a basic analysis of the <em>Priorihominus</em> civilization points to them having a wide interstellar reach, with sufficiently advanced (para-)technology.<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-622990-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-622990-1')">1</a></sup> Large-scale planetary manufacturing might look a bit outside their capabilities &#8212; but we also don't have a timescale! If these are generation ships, then it's likely they were launched in the infancy of their extrasolar civilization.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;and&nbsp;spoiler&nbsp;territory</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Couple things:</p>
<ul>
<li>The &quot;Minotaur&quot; is pattern screamers, which can be linked to their appearance in 1795. Additionally, the debris field is similar to what <a href="/scp-3426">post-3426</a> would look like (albeit on the extreme end of the spectrum).</li>
<li>Something that came before us <em>did</em> have the capacity to create <a href="/scp-002-ex">megastructures</a> beyond the planetary scale.</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>So, if you do want to headcanon a connection, I definitely won't protest it!</p>
<div class="footnotes-footer">
